=== PARITY (vs web RegexTester.tsx) ===
  Data sources -> the web source's ONLY hook is `useTranslation`; it is a pure, synchronous, local
    transform (`new RegExp(...).exec(...)` in a `useMemo`) with NO data hook, NO network, NO cache.
    The native parity therefore binds through a local P1/S8 state holder (RegexTesterModel) that owns
    `pattern` + `flags` + `testString` and DERIVES `outcome` on read (the @Observable analogue of the
    web `useMemo`). The view performs no HTTP — there is none to perform.
  Transform -> RegexEvaluator.evaluate is a faithful port: blank pattern OR test -> `.idle`
    (web `if (!pattern || !testStr) return []`); an INVALID pattern -> `.evaluated([])` (web `catch`
    returns []); with the `g` flag, ALL hits via a `lastIndex`-style loop that BREAKS on the first
    zero-width match (web `if (!m[0]) break`); without `g`, a single first match. UTF-16 offsets
    (NSString == JS string indexing) match `m.index` exactly; `.withTransparentBounds` +
    `.withoutAnchoringBounds` reproduce JS exec-from-lastIndex anchoring (^ stays pinned to the true
    string start unless the `m` flag is set). Verified by EXECUTED XCTest (global multi-hit indices,
    non-global single hit, case-insensitive, multiline-^, non-multiline-^, zero-width break, invalid
    pattern -> [], valid-no-hits).
  Composition -> ToolCard-style header (red `text.magnifyingglass` glyph = web lucide `Regex` + color
    "red" -> `.danger` tone, title + description) · pattern field (web `Input` label `Pattern`, example
    `\d+` -> shared TSTextField) · flags dropdown (web `Select` over `flagOptions` -> shared TSSelect,
    5 presets) · test-string editor (web `Textarea` rows=3 + example overlay) · match-count badge (web
    `Badge` success/neutral by count -> TSBadge) · match rows (web index `Badge` + monospaced rose
    match text + `At Index` -> TSBadge info + mono danger token + muted caption) · idle + no-match
    states. Recharts -> none / Leaflet -> none (no chart/map).
  Shared components -> TSTextField + TSSelect + TSBadge + TSIconBox + TSLabel (Components/UI) for the
    inputs, badges, and header icon; ContentUnavailableView for the idle + no-match states; everything
    else composed from the P1/S9 design tokens (Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing / TSRadius). The
    reusable native `ToolCard` is a separate surface (prompt 0010), so the card chrome is composed
